    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "第六年六月初五日，我坐在家中；犹大的众长老坐在我面前。在那里主耶和华的灵（原文是手）降在我身上。",
      "en": "In the sixth year, in the sixth month, on the fifth of the month,[NOTE:1] as I was sitting in my house with the elders of Judah sitting in front of me, the hand[NOTE:2] of the Sovereign Lord seized me.[NOTE:3]",
      "notes": [
        "The LXX reads “In the sixth year, in the fifth month, on the fifth of the month.” sn In the sixth year, in the sixth month, on the fifth of the month would be September 17, 592 b.c., about fourteen months after the initial vision.",
        "Hand in the OT can refer metaphorically to power, authority, or influence. In Ezekiel God’s hand being on the prophet is regularly associated with communication or a vision from God (3:14, 22; 8:1; 37:1; 40:1).tn Or “power.”",
        "Heb “fell upon me there,” that is, God’s influence came over him."
