    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "他伸出彷佛一只手的样式，抓住我的一绺头发，灵就将我举到天地中间，在　神的异象中，带我到耶路撒冷朝北的内院门口，在那里有触动主怒偶像的坐位，就是惹动忌邪的。",
      "en": "He stretched out the form[NOTE:1] of a hand and grabbed me by a lock of hair on my head. Then a wind[NOTE:2] lifted me up between the earth and sky and brought me to Jerusalem[NOTE:3] by divine visions, to the door of the inner gate that faces north where the statue[NOTE:4] that provokes to jealousy was located.",
      "notes": [
        "The Hebrew term is normally used as an architectural term in describing the pattern of the tabernacle or temple or a representation of it (see Exod 25:8; 1 Chr 28:11).",
        "Or “spirit.” See note on “wind” in 2:2.",
        "For the location of Jerusalem see Map5-B1; Map6-F3; Map7-E2; Map8-F2; Map10-B3; JP1-F4; JP2-F4; JP3-F4; JP4-F4.",
        "Or “image.”"
